{"title":"2026 AMC 8 Regional Problems/Problem 21","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_21\">Problem 21</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Regional_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 21\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Which of the following numbers is a possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> that makes the below statement true?\n\"Randomly select an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />-digit positive integer. The probability that this integer is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/d/83dacecc3f852b6d1fc31accf43e249930c0b27f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"13\" height=\"37\" />.\"\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/7/557ce262b2f4722c079bfb5b413c7df8c15b1676.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 95\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 96\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 97\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 98\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 99$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"394\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Regional_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be a randomly selected <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />-digit positive integer. The total number of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />-digit positive integers is given by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/d/80d573c5a19bb4a9dca58152d73dbc299b22bb43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9 \\times 10^{n-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" />. For a large consecutive range of integers, the probability that a randomly chosen number is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is typically very close to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/d/83dacecc3f852b6d1fc31accf43e249930c0b27f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"13\" height=\"37\" />, but it only equals exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/d/83dacecc3f852b6d1fc31accf43e249930c0b27f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"13\" height=\"37\" /> if the total count of available <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />-digit integers is perfectly divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. Therefore, the statement is true if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> divides the total number of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />-digit integers, meaning <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> must be a divisor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/d/80d573c5a19bb4a9dca58152d73dbc299b22bb43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9 \\times 10^{n-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" />. We can test the given answer choices to see which value satisfies this divisibility condition. For option (B), if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/c/f7cffaeba69a372c654eab221bdcfba58d381016.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 96$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" />, its prime factorization is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/9/1a92996d905bf3b11ddbe70718e00c1a049c46ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$96 = 2^5 \\times 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"92\" height=\"18\" />. We check if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/7/367f6b15d47102fd8fdfc1bafed72c1daeadb35a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$96$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/d/8ad55e6593ff8c007d5ffc912aeda2c69d096df7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9 \\times 10^{95}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/f/08ff9c97907ff9296fdbff24bb089ec925373c4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9 \\times 10^{95} = 3^2 \\times 2^{95} \\times 5^{95}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"197\" height=\"18\" />, the prime factorization contains <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/4/cf4e9faa667ae35d8af5745fb36630df58c275cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{95}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/9/819068968ed60608a91d0c3921d6296964660e9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"17\" />, which easily accommodates the factors <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/7/5b7f45c960c681827d5d03d7b3c30811d3bfd77f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/e/4ce0583e43880c5a6892f664bd95f9a34b53a5f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^1$\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" /> required by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/7/367f6b15d47102fd8fdfc1bafed72c1daeadb35a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$96$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. For the prime options like <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/9/239430b0fc1c7fe38f296a8845ed7446198bda7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$97$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/9/239430b0fc1c7fe38f296a8845ed7446198bda7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$97$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> does not divide <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. For options like <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/1/a313bf06349648df7be807bee95b651604ce7a7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$99$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, its factorization is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/a/44a2037ff1b135a7cabe3d03a7fa1a11c765491d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9 \\times 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> does not divide <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/c/f7cffaeba69a372c654eab221bdcfba58d381016.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 96$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" /> is the only choice that cleanly divides the total count of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />-digit integers.\n</p><p>The correct answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/5/925d78f667c0c5108cc3319969409b9c11729b76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ 96}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"65\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~Icosahedron0288\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Regional_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Regional_Problems\" title=\"2026 AMC 8 Regional Problems\">2026 AMC 8 Regional Problems</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018034359\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.019 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.069 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 203/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6954/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:37407:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018034359 and revision id 291902. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}